		(uuid "91f846aa-9047-4e44-9fd8-cdb1f4cc535e")
	)
	(text "RP2354A robot controller with no radio on the board.\n- USB-C: native USB (UF2, Arduino upload, serial) and charging. The CH224A asks a PD charger for 9 V; plain 5 V works too.\n- BQ25798 charges an internal 3S pack. Charge current is safe with no firmware: the ILIM_HIZ divider caps input at about 0.3 A.\n- Motors and the 5 V buck run from the pack through F1 and the Q1 power switch (VSYS), bypassing the charger's SYS (BATFET 6 A).\n- The MCU's 3.3 V comes from USB alone or from the buck (diode OR), so the board can be programmed with a flat pack.\n- USB-A host (Pico-PIO-USB on GPIO16/17) for a 2.4 GHz controller dongle; U12 switches its VBUS (0.5 A).\n- Three DRV8848 drive six motors; B motors are wired reversed (OUT1 to BOUT2), as in rev 1.\n- GPIO map: MCU & USB sheet. Cross-sheet signals use global labels; rails use power symbols.\nSource of truth: circuit/goosebrain.py (SKiDL). Parts and decisions: circuit/PARTS.md."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
